+## 10. Decision log (this session, 2026-08-12)
+- Resumed from a GitHub snapshot (`github.com/mxxham/k-one-v2`, 3 commits) rather than the Windows filesystem paths in prompt.md (`D:\K-one-v2`, `D:\K-one\k-one\`) — the original PHP source tree is NOT present anywhere accessible in this environment, only the pre-extracted `docs/spec-*.md` files. All S7 work was therefore done strictly from the spec docs + the already-ported Postgres schema, with no ability to diff against a live PHP/MySQL reference (per prompt.md §"Working style" — normally every module is verified against the running PHP API; that step was skipped here and should be done manually against the real `kone-app`/`kone-db` containers before treating S7 as fully parity-verified).
+- `todo.md`/`session.md` in this checkout were stale relative to the actual code: S6 (Inbound) was already fully wired (module + app.module import) and typechecked clean, contradicting the "3 typecheck errors, not wired" note. Corrected both files to match reality rather than trusting the stale checklist.
+- `pickItems`/`ship` implemented as documented in todo.md S7 note above. Two spec ambiguities were resolved conservatively rather than guessed elaborately:
+  1. The "extra picks scan (pick full pallets)" behavior in spec §1.6 was left unimplemented — the spec text itself flags uncertainty about it, and guessing wrong here risks silently over-picking real stock. Only exact per-item FEFO quantities are allocated.
+  2. Spec §1.6 references `outbound_orders.picked_by`/`picked_at`, but the S2-ported schema has no such columns — order-level pick attribution now lives only on the `picklists` row (`created_by`, `confirmed_at`) created inside `pickItems`.
+- Next recommended step: **S8 Picklist module** (`docs/spec-2-outbound-picklist-bintransfer.md` §2) — list/detail/stats/create_from_outbound/confirm/complete/delete/update_item/export_data. Note `pickItems` already creates a `picklists` header + `picklist_items` rows as a side effect, so S8 should read/query that data rather than re-creating it, and `createFromOutbound` needs to coexist with (or replace) that auto-creation path — worth deciding explicitly before writing S8.
 - Working dir note: the v2 source of truth is `D:\K-one-v2\todo.md` + `session.md` (per `prompt.md`). The `todo.md`/`session.md` sitting in the PHP reference repo (`D:\K-one\k-one\todo.md`/`session.md`) are STALE leftovers from the earlier abandoned Express+mysql2 port and should be ignored (do not let them confuse the v2 tracker).
 
